  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Queen Aalia Airport Expansion Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDB had approved US$100 million financing for the project in 2007. This commitment was later reduced by US$15 million, which was syndicated to OFID.  The project aimed at upgrading the airside infrastructure and managing the existing operations at the then terminal along with the construction of a new modern terminal at the same location.  The current financing is a supplementary financing to cater the expected grwoth in actual traffic over the coming years from 7 million passengers to 12 million passengers.</narrative>
  </description>
